// PSS v3.0 LRM — Example 200: Scheduling scenario (page 280)
action read {}
action write {}
monitor m {
  activity {
    schedule {
      do read;
      do write;
   }
  }
}

On all traces, the only realization of the scenario defined by m is set {read, write}, its start time is t1, and
its match time is t4. Note that in the first two traces, the actions are scheduled sequentially, and on the last
two, they overlap.
Now consider monitor m1 and m2 in Example 201, the action trace shown in Figure 44, and the checkpoint
t0.
